# Webview HTML & load handshake

Read [docs/development/WEBVIEW.md](../../docs/development/WEBVIEW.md) before changing webview boot or host→webview messaging.

## Never break these

1. **`getWebviewHtml()`** — hand-written template only; script at **end of `<body>` with `defer`**; never sync script in `<head>`.
2. **Do not regex-replace Vite `index.html`** to inject CSP/scripts (dropping `type="module"` caused 0.4.1 infinite loading).
3. **`hostMessages.ts`** side-effect import in `main.tsx` **before** `createRoot`; ack `loaded` outside React lifecycle when possible.
4. **`__BTVIEW_BOOT__`** — embed serialized document when setting HTML so first paint does not depend on postMessage race.
5. **`WebviewOutboundGate`** — `markNotReady` on every `webview.html` assign; flush on webview `ready`.
6. **`.vscodeignore`** — must ship `webview/dist/assets/` in the VSIX.

## Verify after webview changes

```bash
bash scripts/verify.sh
bash scripts/assert-vsix-webview.sh
```

Open a fixture in BT Graph; Output → BTView must show `ready=true` and `webview loaded document`.
